Validate declared length before allocating byte buffers in ValueReader

CVE-2026-69219: ValueReader.readBytes trusted the 32-bit wire length prefix and
allocated a byte[] of that size before confirming the stream actually contained
that many bytes. A remote (pre-auth) peer could send a small frame declaring a
huge long-string / byte-array length and force a large heap allocation, leading
to denial of service (OutOfMemoryError). readBytes now compares the declared
length against the bytes actually available and throws MalformedFrameException
when the claim exceeds what is present, before any allocation.

Backported from upstream rabbitmq-java-client 6a87a8d (main) /
3882093 (5.x branch, released in v5.33.1).

